# P2-FG1: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`../🦀️component.rs`'s upgraded `DiffCodec` impl, `#region 🔖️TopLevel`) — per the
# P2-W0 census, 100% of stdio's `DiffCodec` impls were still on that shortcut before this pilot
# ladder.
#
# `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `flags u8` (a 4-bit presence mask —
# bit0=`file_description`, bit1=`file_name`, bit2=`file_schema`, bit3=`entities` — `StepDiff` has
# FOUR independently optional top-level fields, same shape dxf's own `DxfDiff` upgraded to this
# same wave, unlike md/json's single `has_value` byte) are the two REAL fixed header fields; each
# PRESENT field's own payload follows as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — genuinely structured,
# field-by-field binary at the Rust layer for every flat record
# (`enc_file_description_bin`/`enc_file_name_bin`/`enc_file_schema_bin` in
# `../../🦀️component.rs`'s `#region 🔖️ValueBinaryCodecs`) and genuinely recursive only where the
# underlying data is (`enc_entities_diff_bin`'s per-entry `enc_entity_diff_bin`/`enc_value_bin`,
# the latter self-recursing on `StepValue::Aggregate`/`TypedValue` via plain Rust function
# recursion). NOT re-modeled field-by-field at THIS protocol-dialect layer for the `entities`
# payload because `Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors on `StepValue`'s self-recursion during
# `walk_protocol` (`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, the recipe's own consolidated gap table — every
# pilot with a self-recursive value type independently hit and worked around the same wall). Same
# honest-boundary treatment the plan prescribes for a compressed/recursive payload segment — opaque
# at the protocol layer, genuinely structured (and round-trip-tested) at the Rust layer.
dialect protocol
protocol stdio.step.diff
version 1
schema stdio.step
start record

framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
